From bf6ee033294f6ee7349fd9f87af56d0ebf0e75be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PePe Amengual <2208324+jamengual@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 13:58:17 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 14/14] kubelet: admit pod-level resources on FreeBSD when the
 kernel enforces them

Pod-level limits are rctl rules on the pod jail, which only bind the
containers (child jails) on kernels with kern.features.rctl_jail_hierarchy.
Admit pods with pod-level resources there (with the PodLevelResources
gate), and reject them with a clear reason otherwise instead of running
them unlimited. Test.
---
 pkg/kubelet/lifecycle/features_freebsd.go     | 63 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../lifecycle/features_freebsd_test.go        | 51 +++++++++++++++
 pkg/kubelet/lifecycle/features_unsupported.go |  2 +-
 3 files changed, 115 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 pkg/kubelet/lifecycle/features_freebsd.go
 create mode 100644 pkg/kubelet/lifecycle/features_freebsd_test.go

diff --git a/pkg/kubelet/lifecycle/features_freebsd.go b/pkg/kubelet/lifecycle/features_freebsd.go
new file mode 100644
index 00000000000..dd99b0c462a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/pkg/kubelet/lifecycle/features_freebsd.go
@@ -0,0 +1,63 @@
